        <item>
            <title>1.0.7</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 21:38:22 +0900</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>105</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.0.7</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
  body { font: -apple-system-body, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; }
  h3 { font-size: 13px; margin: 14px 0 6px; }
  h3:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  ul { margin: 6px 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  li { margin-bottom: 5px; }
  p { margin: 6px 0; }
</style>
<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Fan controls looked frozen in the menu bar.</strong> While an app automation is running, MacBreeze locks the fan settings so the rule stays in charge — but the menu bar never said so. It now tells you which app is in control, and gives you a link straight to App Automations to change it.</li>
<li><strong>The trial-ended notice could be missed.</strong> MacBreeze only checked your licence when it started, so if your trial ended while it was running you weren&#x27;t told until you next restarted it. It now checks once a day.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Privacy</h3>
<p>MacBreeze now records the day your Mac last checked its licence, and whether it&#x27;s on a trial, the free version, or a paid licence, so we can count how many people use it. Nothing about how you use the app is recorded, and the record deletes itself after 90 days without a check-in. The details are in the privacy policy at macbreeze.app.</p>]]></description>
            <enclosure url="https://macbreeze.app/downloads/MacBreeze-1.0.7.dmg" length="3283740" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="bkwz0KdipDLMJR1DYcP87FgNYz/O1DnvRs/ICPltFf+59Ve4vA99QKqpIkEa240b6D7UOzRcDBv045j2p8d8Aw=="/>
